# giving-back — reusable editorial design skill

Produce one **self-contained** `.html` artifact (inline CSS + JS, no build step, no external deps except the Google-Fonts `@import` already in the template) that reproduces the giving-back look exactly. The whole design system — palette, fonts, every component, all animations, the syntax highlighter, and the paged reader — already lives in `assets/template.html`. Your job is to pour the user's content into it as rendered HTML.

## Files (read these first)
- `assets/template.html` — the complete shell: full CSS + JS, a rail/TOC, a cover scene, a `<!--__CHAPTERS__-->` marker, and a send-off scene. **Copy this; keep all CSS and JS byte-for-byte.** Placeholders to fill: `{{TITLE}}`, `{{SUBTITLE}}`, `{{FOOTER_LINE}}`, `{{COVER_KICKER}}`, `{{COLOPHON}}`.
- `references/COMPONENTS.md` — the class vocabulary. Build only from these classes.
- `references/ARCHETYPES.md` — worked section patterns + the two output modes.
- `assets/assemble.py` — inlines per-section fragments at the marker (for large docs).

## Workflow
1. **Read** `assets/template.html`, `references/COMPONENTS.md`, and `references/ARCHETYPES.md`.
2. **Pick the mode** (see ARCHETYPES): a single-page report/explainer, or a multi-section paged guide. Default to the paged guide for anything with more than ~3 sections.
3. **Plan the sections** and build the rail `<nav class="toc">` — one `<a href="#chNN">` per section in order (ch00 = cover, last = send-off), with optional `<div class="railhint">` group dividers. Fill `{{TITLE}}` / `{{SUBTITLE}}` / brand mark / `{{COVER_KICKER}}` / `{{COLOPHON}}` / `{{FOOTER_LINE}}`.
4. **Write each section** as `<section class="chapter" id="chNN">…</section>` using the component vocabulary. Convert the user's content (markdown, notes, code, data, transcripts, whatever) into **rendered** components: headings → `h2.title`/`h3`, emphasis → `<strong>`/`<em>`, lists → `.steps`/cards/`<ul>`, blockquotes → `.quote`, tables/metrics → `.stats`/cards/`.compare`, code fences → `.code` blocks, file paths → `.filetree`. **Never emit literal markdown syntax** (`#`, `**`, `` ` ``, `- `) in the output.
5. **Infographics:** give every substantial section **at least one bespoke hand-drawn animated SVG** (`<svg class="draw">` with the `s-*` helper classes) that diagrams the actual idea — not decoration. This is the signature of the style.
6. **Fill the width:** pair prose with its figures/quotes/code/cards using `.spread` two-column rows. Avoid lone narrow columns with empty space on the right (see the anti-pattern in ARCHETYPES).
7. **Assemble:** inline the sections at `<!--__CHAPTERS__-->`. For a big document, write each section to `chapters/chNN.html` and run `assets/assemble.py` (point its paths at your output dir) — or, for extra scale/quality, fan out parallel subagents (one per section) that each write a fragment, then assemble. For a small one, paste sections directly.
8. **Write** the final single `index.html` to the user's chosen location (or `./giving-back-<slug>/index.html`), then **open it** (`open <path>`), and tell the user the path.

## Hard rules
- **Rendered HTML only — no visible markdown.** The reader must never see `#`, `**`, backticks-as-text, or `- ` bullets. Render everything into the components.
- **Self-contained:** one `.html` file, inline CSS + JS. Inline images as `data:` URIs. Keep the fonts `@import` so Fraunces / Inter / JetBrains Mono render. No frameworks, no CDNs (besides fonts), no build step.
- **Only the template's classes.** No new CSS, no `<style>`, no extra `<script>`. Inline `style=""` is fine.
- **Escape all code** inside `<pre>`/`<code>`/`.filetree`: `&`→`&amp;`, `<`→`&lt;`, `>`→`&gt;`. A raw `<`/`>` in a code block breaks the page.
- **Animations on:** `reveal` (+ `d1…d6` stagger) on most blocks; `draw` on every `<svg>`. The bundled JS wires reveal-on-show, SVG draw-in, the syntax highlighter, and the paged navigation — do not re-implement them.
- **Section ids match the TOC.** Every `<section id="chNN">` has a matching `#chNN` rail link; the last section id matches the last TOC entry.
- Faithful to the source content; bespoke, on-theme SVGs; editorial, confident voice.

## Quick self-check before delivering
- 0 raw markdown tokens in the body · every section has ≥1 animated SVG · code blocks escaped · `.spread` used so no big empty right gaps · TOC ids all resolve · `<div>`/`<svg>`/`<section>` balanced · single self-contained file that opens offline.
