-            <li>Prompt the agent to add a test for <code>sanitize_table_name</code> covering a parenthesized filename and run pytest again. Require all existing tests plus the new case to pass.</li>
-            <li>Because the server start has repeated at least three times, have the agent create <code>.claude/commands/start.md</code> containing exactly <code>sh ./scripts/start.sh 300s</code>. Restart the agent and prove <code>/start</code> works from a cold session.</li>
-            <li>Exit to a plain shell and run <code>claude -p "/tools"</code>. Observe the reusable prompt run headlessly and return its result.</li>
+        <section class="lab-box" id="lab-fix"><h3 class="lab-box__title">Lab 3 · Repair and close the test loop · 25 points</h3><ul class="lab-box__meta"><li>20–30 min</li><li>Behavioral grading</li><li>Preserve stale DB as evidence</li></ul>
+          <ol>
+            <li>Prompt <code>resolve: replace bad chars and escape</code>. Review the agent’s sanitizer for four behaviors: extension handling, invalid-character replacement, legal leading character, and nonempty fallback.</li>
+            <li>Have the agent write focused tests covering a parenthesized name, a leading digit, and a name made only of invalid characters. It must run the focused tests and then <code>uv run pytest</code> itself.</li>
+            <li>Stop services. If <code>app/server/db/database.db</code> exists, preserve it by moving it to <code>database.before-lab.db</code>. Do not delete it. The stale table exists because pandas created it before PRAGMA failed.</li>
+            <li>Restart inside the agent and upload the file again. Verify a valid identifier (the video implementation yields <code>orders__32_</code>), 32 rows, and 7 columns. Use <code>GET /api/schema</code> for a deterministic keyless check.</li>
+            <li>Capture the final full-suite result: at least 35 tests pass, possibly more if the new cases are parametrized.</li>
           </ol>
-          <div class="checkpoint"><strong>Checkpoint 3.</strong> The five-file trace matches grep; pytest runs inside the agent before and after the new test; <code>/start</code> works cold; and programmable mode returns the tools list to the shell.</div>
-          <div class="lab-box__pass"><h4>Pass criteria</h4><ul><li>The type trace is exact, not approximate.</li><li>The agent owns test execution and correction.</li><li><code>start.md</code> is identified as your lab artifact, not shipped source.</li><li>You can state the ADW formula while the headless prompt runs.</li></ul></div>
+          <aside class="checkpoint"><p class="callout__label">Checkpoint D</p><p>Submit sanitizer diff, test diff, agent-run outputs, preserved database path, and 32×7 schema evidence. The optional “latest delivery” query requires an external provider and is not graded.</p></aside>
         </section>
 
-        <section class="lab-box" id="lab-kpi">
-          <h3 class="lab-box__title">Lab 2.4 · Leverage ablation and KPI journal</h3>
-          <ul class="lab-box__meta"><li>20–40 min stretch</li><li>diagnosis</li><li>graded reflection</li></ul>
-          <ol class="lab-box__steps">
-            <li><strong>Ablation:</strong> using safe repository controls, preserve your working diff, then restore <code>server.py</code> and <code>file_processor.py</code> to the before-state. Run the server outside the agent with no stdout and ask a fresh agent to fix the CSV upload bug. Record the wasted exploration without coaching it.</li>
-            <li>Restore the stdout and sanitizer changes, run the service where the agent sees output, and repeat. Name the exact levers whose removal caused the first run to flail.</li>
-            <li><strong>KPI journal:</strong> for three prompts, record size, attempts, current streak, and presence. A broken streak requires a missing-lever sentence before the next prompt.</li>
-            <li><strong>Optional context drill:</strong> through the agent, extend <code>prime.md</code> to read <code>core/data_models.py</code>. Compare a fresh type question before and after. Name the lever.</li>
-            <li><strong>Optional naming drill:</strong> have the agent rename one weak request type to an information-dense name, run the tests itself, and retrace the new name. Do not broaden into an architecture refactor.</li>
-            <li><strong>Optional architecture audit:</strong> score TAC-2 against all nine checks from the architecture section, cite real paths, and write the gap list only. Do not refactor; this is the read-only S5 drill from the source lab.</li>
+        <section class="lab-box" id="lab-trace"><h3 class="lab-box__title">Lab 4 · Trace structure and abstract repetition · 25 points</h3><ul class="lab-box__meta"><li>20–30 min</li><li>15 points trace</li><li>10 points template/programmatic call</li></ul>
+          <ol>
+            <li>Open a brand-new agent with zero conversation history. Ask it to trace <code>DatabaseSchemaResponse</code> through files, functions, and purpose, using a structured output format.</li>
+            <li>Independently search the repository. Verify the same five files: Python model, server route, TypeScript types, API client, and spec. Explain each role.</li>
+            <li>After starting the server at least three times, tell the agent to create <code>.claude/commands/start.md</code> with the course’s prompt text <code>sh ./scripts/start.sh 300s</code>. Restart the agent and verify <code>/start</code> from a cold session. Treat the 300s text as command-parser input, not proof that <code>start.sh</code> accepts a duration argument.</li>
+            <li>Exit to the shell and run <code>claude -p "/tools"</code>. Capture the returned tool list and shell prompt. Explain why this is only an ADW seed: there is not yet an arbitrary wrapper plus autonomous trigger.</li>
           </ol>
-          <div class="lab-box__pass"><h4>Pass criteria</h4><ul><li>Your reflection distinguishes a bad model outcome from a missing-lever system.</li><li>The journal contains numeric observations, not “felt faster.”</li><li>You do not refactor the architecture or build a full ADW in this lesson.</li></ul></div>
         </section>
 
-        <aside class="callout callout--why">
-          <p class="callout__label">Troubleshooting the lab</p>
-          <ul>
-            <li>If the inside start exits immediately, stop the outside process first; the ports are already occupied.</li>
-            <li>If old and new tables appear together, remove the stale database before the final upload.</li>
-            <li>If the service dies after five minutes, the course-era timeout behaved as configured. Rerun or use the minted command.</li>
-            <li>If startup exits early, confirm <code>app/server/.env</code> exists. Its error text is itself a stdout-lever example.</li>
-            <li>At least one API key is required for natural-language queries. Course-era model IDs may need an agent-performed update if an account no longer supports them.</li>
-          </ul>
-        </aside>
+        <section class="lab-box" id="lab-final"><h3 class="lab-box__title">Final rubric and troubleshooting</h3>
+          <div class="comparison"><article class="comparison__card comparison__card--agentic"><div class="comparison__head"><h3>Pass evidence</h3><p>Every item required.</p></div><div class="comparison__body"><ul><li>10/10 audit facts</li><li>Exact planted failure and line chain</li><li>Agent-observed stdout, no human relay</li><li>Valid 32×7 upload and green suite</li><li>Verified five-file type trace</li><li>Cold <code>/start</code> and headless tool list</li><li>Final diff preserved for review</li></ul></div></article><article class="comparison__card"><div class="comparison__head"><h3>Common stalls</h3><p>Diagnose the starting state.</p></div><div class="comparison__body"><ul><li>Outside server still owns ports</li><li>300-second run expired normally</li><li><code>.env</code> missing so startup exits</li><li>Stale table remains in old DB</li><li>Type trace costs substantial tokens</li><li>Optional query lacks a valid key</li></ul></div></article></div>
+          <aside class="callout callout--why"><p class="callout__label">No destructive ablation in the graded tree</p><p>If you want to compare the blind before-state with the leveraged after-state, use a second disposable standalone clone. Do not use checkout/reset to erase the working diff and then assume an unstated stash can restore it.</p></aside>
+        </section>
