       <section class="chapter-section" id="mastery">
         <span class="section-number">14</span>
         <h2 class="section-title">Cumulative mastery · retrieve, diagnose, transfer</h2>
-        <p class="section-lead">Close every earlier section. Answer aloud or on paper before opening the details. A definition that cannot guide a failed run earns half credit.</p>
-
-        <h3>Round 1 · The system and tactic</h3>
-        <section class="retrieval-quiz" aria-label="Cumulative retrieval round one">
-          <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">1. Name both leverage families and all twelve points.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>In-agent: context, model, prompt, tools. Through-agent: standard out, types, documentation, tests, architecture, plans, templates, ADWs.</p></details></div>
-          <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">2. State Tactic #2 and its litmus question.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Adopt Your Agent’s Perspective. With my agent’s core four, is it possible to complete the task I have given it?</p></details></div>
-          <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">3. Name the five phase-two SDLC steps and explain why Dan bets on them.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Plan, code, test, review, document. They are durable engineering structures beneath model and tool churn.</p></details></div>
-          <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">4. Define bad agentic code and state the planted bug with path and line.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Code that hides failures from the agent’s observable streams. orders_(32) reaches <code>PRAGMA table_info({table_name})</code> at <code>app/server/core/file_processor.py:26</code> and breaks SQLite syntax.</p></details></div>
-        </section>
-
-        <h3>Round 2 · Runtime, naming, and navigation</h3>
-        <section class="retrieval-quiz" aria-label="Cumulative retrieval round two">
-          <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">5. Which command inspects the tool roster, and which Bash parameter enables the course-era inside-agent server run?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p><code>/tools</code>; the timeout parameter, used for a 300-second run.</p></details></div>
-          <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">6. Reproduce the two short diagnostic/repair prompts and explain why they work.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>“Any issues with the server?” then “resolve: replace bad chars and escape.” They work because stdout exists, the service runs inside the agent, and the agent has inspection and editing tools.</p></details></div>
-          <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">7. Expand IDK and trace <code>DatabaseSchemaResponse</code> through five files.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Information dense keyword; data_models.py → server.py → types.d.ts → api/client.ts → specs/init_nlq_to_sql_to_table.md.</p></details></div>
