+# TAC-2 chapter status — The 12 Leverage Points
+
+Status: **CHAPTERED — ready for Claude cross-review**
+
+## Deliverables
+
+- Chapter: vol-1-tac/02-the-12-leverage-points.html
+- Chapter CSS: vol-1-tac/02-the-12-leverage-points.assets.css
+- Source extract: _extracts/tac-2-the-12-leverage-points/
+- Hub: index.html linked and aggregate progress updated without overwriting the concurrent TAC-4 chapter
+- Curriculum: data/curriculum.json set to chaptered with extract, chapter, estimates, and two approved overlays
+
+## Measured density
+
+- Visible-text estimate: **11,867 words** (HTML tags, CSS, and progress script excluded)
+- Print-equivalent estimate: **44–50 pages**, depending on frame placement and browser print pagination
+- Teaching cycles: **12 of 12**, each with Hook → Picture → Story → Name → Worked example → You try → Fail/fix → Current Practice → Retrieval → Teach-back
+- Course frames: **12 of 12**, all full-width breakout cards with timestamps and explanatory captions
+- Cumulative retrieval: **16 of 16** extract questions included
+- Current-practice YouTube overlays: **2** (hGg3nWp7afg, X2ciJedw2vU); deferred ADW video intentionally omitted
+
+## Accuracy locks preserved
+
+- The committed repository is shown as the broken before-state: zero stdout prints in server.py and no sanitizer in file_processor.py.
+- The stdout diff, sanitizer, sanitizer test, and start.md are labeled as demo/lab-created artifacts.
+- The exact planted failure is orders_(32) reaching PRAGMA table_info({table_name}) at app/server/core/file_processor.py:26.
+- No CLAUDE.md is claimed to exist in TAC-2; README plus /prime carry the briefing role.
+- adws/ and agents/ are described as empty scaffolding, not implemented workflows.
+- The course-era tool roster and 300-second foreground timeout are separated from the current background-task pattern.
+- Labs stay inside tac/tac-2 and exclude external-repo work, architecture refactors, MCP construction, frontend agent testing, and a full ADW build.
+
+## Verification completed
+
+- All local stylesheet, generated-image, and twelve frame paths resolve from the chapter directory.
+- Every desktop rail and mobile TOC anchor resolves to an existing section.
+- Every major idea contains all ten required pedagogical moves.
+- Curriculum JSON parses.
+- Hub progress reflects all currently chaptered work in the shared workspace at verification time: TAC-1, TAC-2, and TAC-4.
+- HTML uses the shared light design tokens, base, components, and gold chapter layout; body copy remains 17px through shared tokens.
+
+## Open questions for Claude review
+
+1. Is 11,867 visible words sufficiently dense beside TAC-1’s 13,100 estimate, given this chapter also carries twelve large frames, two designed diagrams, a five-part lab, and sixteen cumulative retrieval items?
+2. Should the reused X2ciJedw2vU Agent Skills overlay remain here, or should chapter stitching enforce zero cross-chapter video reuse? If one overlay must be dropped, drop this one first.
+3. Does the hub’s latest-feature choice remain TAC-4 while the aggregate counts include TAC-2, or should a later editorial pass choose a deterministic featured-chapter policy?
+4. Should the course-era exact prompt “sh ./scripts/start.sh, 300s” retain Dan’s comma form everywhere, or should review normalize explanatory prose to the runnable shell form while keeping the quoted lesson prompt exact?
+5. Do reviewers want a second current-practice note on permission modes/hooks, or is the lab permissions audit plus tool/current-practice notes enough to avoid overloading the chapter?
+
+## Suggested cross-review focus
+
+- Compare every claim with extract.md, extract.json, lab-spec.md, and outdated-vs-current.md.
+- Confirm captions match the visible content of all twelve frames.
+- Inspect print pagination around full-width frames and the long lab.
+- Run the lab from a clean TAC-2 checkout if API credentials and token budget are available.
