177:        <div class="move move--current"><p class="move-label">8 · Current practice</p><aside class="current-practice"><p class="current-practice__source">Observability, not print worship</p><p>At larger scale, structured logs, trace IDs, filtered session files, and error summaries can replace ad hoc prints. The invariant is direct machine-readable access to the evidence that narrows the state space.</p></aside></div>
193:        <div class="move move--current"><p class="move-label">8 · Current practice</p><aside class="current-practice"><p class="current-practice__source">Operational principle</p><p>Whether the runtime is local, containerized, or remote, arrange for the acting agent to retrieve the relevant output and checks without a human paraphrasing them. Human review remains; human relay is the avoidable bottleneck.</p></aside></div>
241:        <div class="move move--current"><p class="move-label">8 · Current practice</p><aside class="current-practice"><p class="current-practice__source">Progressive disclosure</p><p>Keep a concise always-read project guide, then route agents to deeper domain or vendor docs only when a task needs them. Local-first does not mean load-everything-first.</p></aside></div>

